Open the touch selection menu below the selection under the shell's top bar.

The quick menu (Cut / Copy / Select all) goes above the selection unless
that would leave the screen. On a phone the shell's status and address bars
cover the top of the window, which still counts as on screen, so for a
field near the top of the page the menu opened under the address bar, half
hidden. On OHOS, where there is no room for it between the selection and
the top of the visible page, the anchor is stretched to the top of the
screen so the bubble goes below the selection instead.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-touch-menu-below-shell-bar.patch

